    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R62"],
      "pins": ["R62.1", "R62.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "Net-(U15-Y)"],
      "observed": "R62 is listed with value 10 and is SPICE-modelled as 10 ohms, but it is used as a pullup from +3V3 to U15-Y and its MPN is the same 10k resistor part used by the neighboring 10K pullups.",
      "expected": "R62 should be a 10k pullup (consistent with MPN 0603WAF1002T5E and the role of the net), not a 10 ohm resistor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "R62 | 10 | Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric | MotorController:TAYLOR_RESISTOR |  | LCSC=C25804, MPN= 0603WAF1002T5E"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(U15-Y) : R45.2(passive) R62.2(2,passive) U15.4(Y,output) U35.2(A,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R62 +3V3 Net-_U15-Y_ 10"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A 10 ohm pullup would force hundreds of milliamps when U15 sinks the node, likely overheating or damaging the buffer and corrupting the e-stop/LED signal chain.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U3", "U12", "R16", "R17", "C19"],
      "pins": ["U3.4", "U12.3"],
      "nets": ["+5V", "FB"],
      "observed": "U3.4, the LM2576 feedback pin, appears on both the +5V rail and the FB net. The FB net is also the TPS61040 boost feedback divider node for +12V.",
      "expected": "The LM2576 fixed-output FB pin should be connected to its own output/sense node, not shorted to the TPS61040 feedback divider. U12 FB should see only the +12V divider.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U3.4(FB,input), U6.6(SENSE,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "FB : C19.2(passive) R16.2(passive) R17.1(passive) U12.3(FB,passive) U3.4(FB,input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "U3 | LM2576HVS-5 | Package_TO_SOT_SMD:TO-263-5_TabPin3 | Regulator_Switching:LM2576HVS-5 | 5V 3A, SIMPLE SWITCHER® Step-Down Voltage Regulator, High Voltage Input, TO-263"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The 5V output is tied to the boost LED-driver feedback divider; the TPS61040 FB pin is forced near 5V and will not regulate the +12V rail correctly, and the LM2576 feedback path is disturbed.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["D30", "R60"],
      "pins": ["D30.4", "D30.2", "R60.1", "R60.2"],
      "nets": ["ESTOP_OUT", "Net-(D30-K2)", "/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV"],
      "observed": "For the second LED inside D30, the anode D30.4 is connected directly to ESTOP_OUT, while the cathode D30.2 is connected through R60 back to the same ESTOP_OUT net.",
      "expected": "An LED indicator tied to ESTOP_OUT should have its two terminals at different potentials, for example anode on the LED supply and cathode through R60 to ESTOP_OUT, so the LED can light when the signal state changes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "cm4-robot:LED_Dual_KKAA | Dual LED, cathodes on pins 1 and 3 | pins: 1=K1(input) 2=K2(input) 3=A1(input) 4=A2(input)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "/LED_3.3V_POWER_NONINV : D28.2(A,passive) D29.2(A,passive) D30.3(A1,input) D8.2(A,passive) Q10.1(G,input) R58.2(2,passive) U34.4(Y,output) U7.5(OE,input)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The second D30 LED has no voltage across it and will not function as an e-stop/status indicator.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show multiple likely deviations: a 10 ohm pullup where the MPN and circuit role indicate 10k, the LM2576 feedback pin shorted into the TPS61040 +12V feedback divider, and a D30 LED whose terminals are tied to the same ESTOP_OUT net."
}

